==English==

===Etymology===
From the present participle of {{der|en|fro|afier}}, from {{der|en|LL.|affidare}}. Related to {{m|en|affidavit}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/əˈfaɪ.ənt/}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪənt}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|legal}} The individual witness whose statement is contained in an affidavit or sworn deposition.
#: ''Further '''affiant''' sayeth naught.'' (A centuries-old statement that is still used on some legal documents as the final declaration prior to the affiant's signature.)

